something I often hear from people who haven’t&nbsp;
watched One Piece for more than 10 minutes.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.200
In my last video I made my case why Luffy is&nbsp;
the the best Shounen Hero from a storytelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.640
perspective, and since you guys kept asking for&nbsp;
it, today, we’re gonna change that to a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.280
personal perspective. Basically, why I&nbsp;
personally find Luffy to be a very relatable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.200
person &amp; a fantastic role model. This video, for&nbsp;
obvious reasons, will be a lot more subjective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.520
because different people are drawn to different&nbsp;
personalities. Nonetheless I’m convinced I’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.800
found the reason, why so many people are drawn&nbsp;
to him and the overall story so much. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.240
after watching this video, the next time someone&nbsp;
tells you that Luffy sucks, you’ll know exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.640
what to tell them. Also, if this is the second&nbsp;
or third video of mine that you have watched,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.200
this is the YouTube gods telling you to subscribe.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.080
Oh, and just as a quick caveat, because I saw a&nbsp;
lot of people commenting about this in part I,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.160
when I talk about Luffy as a Hero, I&nbsp;
mean it in the literary sense of Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.640
being the hero of the story, not Luffy&nbsp;
running around with All Might. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:14.240
while I personally think Luffy is the most well&nbsp;
written Shounen hero, I obviously haven’t read&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.840
or watched every single shounen. Plus there&nbsp;
are a ton of other protagonists I aboszultley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:26.400
love - looking at you Itadori. So don’t take&nbsp;
this as an attack on your favorite show.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.680
Okay, so first of all, let’s deal with the common&nbsp;
points of criticism about Luffy as a person.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:43.280
Is Luffy dumb? Well, the short answer is - yes.&nbsp;
Luffy is clearly not gonna win a Nobel price in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.560
chemistry any time soon. In fact he knows&nbsp;
close to nothing about science or politics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.360
And even on a much more fundamental level,&nbsp;
he’s not even able to see through even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.240
most basic disguises. So basically, when&nbsp;
looking at it from an academic perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.880
Luffy is not exactly to smartest cookie in&nbsp;
the jar. And for someone who only follows One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:09.520
Piece very sporadically, it’s only natural&nbsp;
that this idiotic &amp; naive side of Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.720
seems to be all there is to him. However&nbsp;
there are many forms of intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.880
and while Luffy clearly lacks in a number of&nbsp;
areas, he is an absolute genius when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.160
social and emotional intelligence, that I would&nbsp;
argue is just as crucial as intellectual one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.120
And I think that’s exactly what sets him apart&nbsp;
from many other heroes. Luffy is well aware of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:37.040
his true self and that of those around him right&nbsp;
from the start. He knows exactly what he can and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:49.840
can’t do. That’s exactly why he gathered a&nbsp;
crew of people that made up for his weaknesses.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.760
Luffy’s emotional intelligence allow him to&nbsp;
understand more about the people around him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.360
than they do about themselves. He is fantastic at&nbsp;
identifying people’s true feelings and intentions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.480
- What’s driving them and what’s holding them&nbsp;
back. And he does so with friends and foes alike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:12.480
Luffy might be bad at cooking or navigating or&nbsp;
fixing things, but he he knows people. And that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:20.160
is arguable the most important skill any leader&nbsp;
needs. So, is Luffy idiotic at times? Sure, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.120
I would argue he’s not idiotic to the point where&nbsp;
it gets annoying. This is my personal impression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.000
but for example with Naruto, especially in&nbsp;
Shippuden, I often got annoyed with his attitude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.000
towards things. Compare running after Sasuke&nbsp;
without question with Usopp leaving the crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.840
Or how Naruto stubbornly keeps fighting&nbsp;
enemies that are too strong for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.760
only to get a mid-fight power-up,&nbsp;
while Luffy knows exactly when it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.160
time to run. No matter if against&nbsp;
Aokiji, Kizaru, Smoker or Big Mom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.080
Luffy, as the leader is prepared to&nbsp;
buy time or even die for his friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:09.120
but he’s fully aware that the best bet is to&nbsp;
avoid a confrontation. And whenever Luffy actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.440
decides to stay behind and fight, as Naruto&nbsp;
does, he actually has to face real consequences.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.840
And this brings me to the second big point of&nbsp;
criticism: Luffy has no character development.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.360
I already stated in the last video that Luffy’s&nbsp;
arc is about becoming a better leader. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:35.360
change in personality is slow, but inarguably&nbsp;
there. The reason for that is, that Luffy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:40.480
already a very good leader by nature, that&nbsp;
pulls others up, instead of pushing them down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:48.160
like many other characters in the story. Luffy&nbsp;
build trust with people extremely fast, one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:54.320
most fundamental elements of being a good leader.&nbsp;
He leads by example and has a very clear vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.600
that aligns with the dreams of his crew, so that&nbsp;
it is incredibly easy to follow him. Put simply,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.920
Luffy is someone you would want to&nbsp;
lead the way when shit goes down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:09.040
as he does every single arc of the story. So,&nbsp;
having all these natural leadership traits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:14.640
already, what Luffy’s personal development&nbsp;
is really focused on is loosing a bit of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:23.840
naivety and carelessness, so he can be a captain&nbsp;
that can protect his crew and their dreams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.520
Moments like Sabaody or Marineford are all&nbsp;
about that concept. However, since Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.960
naivety and carelessness are also a big reason&nbsp;
why he’s able to do all the crazy things he does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:44.160
he can’t loose these traits completely&nbsp;
either, so he never stops dreaming.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.880
And for all his goofing off and recklessness,&nbsp;
Luffy takes his duties as the captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:55.120
very seriously. This is shown when Luffy&nbsp;
listens to Vivi and takes a peaceful approach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.880
instead of just beating up everyone at Drum&nbsp;
Island. Or when he listens to Iceberg and decides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:07.520
to get a new ship, despite being very attached to&nbsp;
Going Merry. Or when he decides to fight Aokiji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:13.440
one-on-one, despite being vastly outmatched, to&nbsp;
save his crew. And of course, when he takes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:19.840
hard decision to disband the crew for two years,&nbsp;
so that they can all grow and come back stronger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:24.800
All of this shows certain maturity on Luffy's&nbsp;
part and his ability to make tough decisions.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.680
As a result, you have only very&nbsp;
little character development.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.240
Rather we see Luffy giving massive&nbsp;
character development to those around him.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.040
And now that we have countered the two biggest&nbsp;
arguments against Luffy as a person, let’s look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:47.840
what I believe makes him so incredibly relatable&nbsp;
and actually a wonderful role model to follow.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:03.200
Fulfilling the trope of the typical Shounen&nbsp;
Hero, Luffy has a number extremely cool traits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:07.920
He’s basically fearless, to the point where&nbsp;
he doesn’t even fear death. He has incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:14.240
physical power &amp; uses it creatively, another form&nbsp;
of intelligence by the way. He has a ridiculous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:20.720
level of pain endurance and also an iron will,&nbsp;
that never seems to falter. All of these traits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:28.320
are really cool to watch and see in action, but&nbsp;
are they actually relatable? Heroes like Goku&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:35.120
and Ichigo share these same traits, but they are&nbsp;
so detached from what being a real human being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.680
is, that it’s hard to actually identify&nbsp;
with. Much rather I think it’s exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:45.360
those characteristics in Luffy that make him so&nbsp;
lovable, that seem to be the opposite of cool.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.000
Take for instance what we talked about earlier:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:54.160
Luffy has a lot of weaknesses and actually&nbsp;
gets his ass handed to him quite a lot. Having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.160 --> 00:08:00.160
weaknesses and failing? Now that’s something&nbsp;
everyone can relate to. And so it’s the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.040
that Luffy deals with these faults, that make him&nbsp;
stand out to me. The fact that he works hard and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:10.640
isn’t afraid to fail over and over, and that&nbsp;
he doesn’t mind openly admitting his faults to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:16.880
neither himself nor his friends, is what I&nbsp;
find so admirable. I also absolutely love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:22.480
Luffy’s child-like curiosity and joy, something&nbsp;
that especially as an adult I think deep down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:28.560
everyone misses. Luffy also has an extremely&nbsp;
strong and straightforward identity. He knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:35.360
what he wants, what he values and who he is and&nbsp;
in the process doesn’t take himself too seriously.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.640
That’s an incredibly attractive trait to have&nbsp;
as it speaks for a lot of self-confidence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:46.080
a sense of purpose and clarity about one-self&nbsp;
that I personally find absolutely admirable.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:52.080
But maybe the most fascinating trait about&nbsp;
Luffy, is his extreme altruism. Luffy ties his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:57.920
own happiness tightly to that of his friends.&nbsp;
Unlike Blackbeard, becoming pirate king on his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:03.680
means nothing to him. His strong sense of justice&nbsp;
and fairness always push him to help those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:09.280
need a light in the dark. Due to his compassion&nbsp;
and empathy, his identity is based around saving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:15.120
people. Not only physically, but especially&nbsp;
mentally. And he does so with incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:21.120
fairness. Because Luffy is able to judge&nbsp;
people purely by their character and not their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.240
appearance and manner. And I would argue that&nbsp;
that’s a skill we could all use a lot more of.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.000
Every single straw hat is someone&nbsp;
with an incredibly kind heart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.480
no matter how much they might have looked like&nbsp;
a villain, as for instance with Robin or Franky.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:39.920
Before meeting Luffy, every single straw hat&nbsp;
had been stuck in a really dark place mentally.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.240
And every single one of them, Luffy&nbsp;
pulls out of that darkness, rekindles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:49.280
their dreams &amp; gives them a worthy leader to&nbsp;
follow as well as a family to support them.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:55.600
In a way, Luffy is a sort of Buddha, that is&nbsp;
kind, doesn’t lie, is pure of heart and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.600 --> 00:10:01.120
guiding others on their path. Since I meditate&nbsp;
myself, I want to use the term carefully here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.720
as it’s pretty controversial. But one&nbsp;
could argue that Luffy has actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.640
reached a certain state of enlightenment,&nbsp;
where he is living in the here and now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.320
with an incredible sense of clarity &amp; mindfulness.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:17.200
It’s these traits, that for me make&nbsp;
Luffy someone who’s not only relatable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:22.560
but someone who encourages me to be a better,&nbsp;
kinder and happier version of myself. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:31.200
I hope that this video brought you some&nbsp;
joy as well. Thanks for watching. Peace.

